[[4495,1698,"None of the Carers employed at Hibiscus House had any training in CPR","lack of CPR training among carers",""],[4496,1698,"There was no Registered First Aider at the premises","absence of registered first aider",""],[4497,1698,"There was no defibrillator on site","lack of defibrillator availability",""],[4498,1698,"There was no emergency bell/alarm or telephone in the residents' dining room","absence of emergency communication device",""],[4499,1698,"Post inquest, the Coroner noted the CQC Inspection report for Hibiscus House Domiciliary Care Agency dated July 2019 which rated the facility as 'requiring improvement'","inadequate CQC follow-up on improvement plan",""],[11149,4286,"buzzer/alarm in the deceased room had been removed/disabled due to a previous incident where the deceased had attempted to place the cord around her neck","lack of emergency call system",""],[11150,4286,"observations were not recorded as to when they actually took place or what was observed.","unrecorded observations",""],[11151,4286,"deceased preferred to have her bedroom door left open but this did not form part of her care plan","door status not managed",""],[11152,4286,"other resident suspected to have been the assailant was a new referral to the home and that there was a lack of information on her admission","inadequate risk assessment",""],[11153,4286,"obvious signs of an injury to Edna's head in the form of the injury to her eye which resulted in bruising and swelling","head injury not managed",""],[11154,4286,"no medical review was sought until an ambulance was called on 29/11/19 when the deceased became unresponsive","delayed medical review",""],[12277,4743,"Evidence emerged during the inquest that there was inadequate communication between the Hospital and occupational therapist to resolve the issue in a timely manner which resulted in a minimal exercise/mobility regime being implemented","inadequate communication between Hospital and occupational therapist",""],[12278,4743,"Although it is recognised some bed bound exercises were completed there was insufficient urgency amongst those professionals involved to resolve the matter as quickly as possible and thereby reduce the risks of complications, including pulmonary embolism from developing","insufficient urgency among professionals to resolve mobility issues",""],[13663,5316,"Evidence emerged during the inquest that there was a previous incident at the same location involving a member of public who narrowly escaped falling to the road below in April 2017 in similar circumstances.","previous incident at same location involving member of public narrowly escaping falling to road below",""],[13664,5316,"Evidence also emerged during the inquest that an alarm would be activated if the fire exit was used. It appears that security guards employed to deal with unauthorised use of the fire exit failed to attend.","security guards failing to attend unauthorised fire exit use",""]]